desc: Image Conscious Stereo Image / MS Matrix (mda Image port) by chmaha
tags: stereo width mid-side imager matrix utility
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A stereo image adjuster and mid-side matrix. Mode sets what goes in and what comes out:
  SM->LR decodes side (left input) and mid (right input) to left/right, MS->LR decodes mid (left) and side (right),
  LR->LR adjusts an ordinary stereo signal, and LR->MS encodes left/right to mid (left output) and side (right output).
  S Width sets the side level (-200 to +200 %, negative flips the side polarity, 0 is mono) and S Pan moves the side
  signal between the channels; M Level and M Pan do the same for the mid signal. Output trims the level by up to 20 dB.
  The display shows the resulting mixing matrix: how much of each input reaches each output.
  Fix: in the original, LR->MS encoded the side as (R-L)/2 while the decoding modes expect (L-R)/2, so encoding and
  decoding again swapped left and right. LR->MS now outputs the standard side (L-R)/2; everything else is unchanged.
  Ported from mda Image by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
